 "_comment": "A one-line cat: ONE designed path, smoothed with centripetal Catmull-Rom. Not an outline with details bridged on -- that reads as glue. The line enters along the ground, climbs the chest, rounds the ears, makes a single excursion through the face (muzzle, both slanted eyes, back down the muzzle), drops into the legs with a deliberate crossing, and leaves as the tail. The head is rotated -12 degrees about the neck for the tilt, tapered over three points at each join so the body line does not kink."
